57
00:03:21,760 --> 00:03:25,400
transmission along an axon, and how it limits

58
00:03:25,400 --> 00:03:28,480
the number of impulses that can be sent each second.

59
00:03:29,120 --> 00:03:33,160
Behind the active region, sodium channels are inactivated, so

60
00:03:33,160 --> 00:03:35,920
local currents cannot restart an action potential there.

61
00:03:36,520 --> 00:03:40,540
Ahead, the membrane is still at rest, so it can reach threshold.

62
00:03:41,360 --> 00:03:45,200
Because each patch must recover before it can fire again, there

63
00:03:45,200 --> 00:03:49,220
is a minimum time between spikes, and that limits firing frequency.

